================================================================================

JudoAdministración is source-available software, NOT open source.

The software has two parts, licensed differently:

  · The DESKTOP APPLICATION (installed on the workstations) is free of charge and
    unlimited: any number of machines, users, events or time, for any purpose including
    commercial use, with no registration or prior authorisation.

  · The SERVER SERVICE (the one that stores the competition data and that the
    workstations connect to) requires a Server Licence issued by the copyright holder.
    That licence MAY BE PAID and must be requested from the copyright holder by writing
    to jcotolisanfelix@gmail.com; its terms and price, if any, are agreed case by
    case. See clause 2 of the binding Spanish text.

  This change was introduced in version 1.1 of this licence and is not retroactive:
  each copy of the software is governed by the licence that accompanied it (clause 13.2).

You MAY also: read and study the source code of the whole program; and redistribute the
software verbatim, free of charge, with all notices intact.

You MAY NOT: modify the software or create derivative works; distribute modified
versions; republish the source code in any repository other than the official one; keep,
develop or promote an independent fork; reuse portions of the code in other projects;
remove copyright and authorship notices; or tamper with, forge or circumvent the server
licence file.

Modifications must be proposed to the official repository. A technical fork is allowed
only to prepare such a proposal and must not be maintained as an independent project.
All contributions are subject to the project's Contributor License Agreement (CLA.md),
which assigns the economic rights in the contribution exclusively to the copyright holder.

The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind.

